    "severity": "moderate",
    "reachable": "uncertain",
    "assessment": "minimatch 10.2.6 is installed through Expo fingerprinting and TypeScript ESLint tooling. The advisory requires an attacker-controlled glob pattern with optimizationLevel >= 2. Reviewed local call sites use default options or dot matching; no such attacker-controlled pattern was found. Expo is classified on the Android, production, and web surfaces because it is a runtime dependency; actual fingerprint use appears to be build tooling. Exposure remains uncertain.",
    "mitigation": "Build and lint patterns remain repository-controlled; CI has bounded jobs. These controls limit exposure but do not fix the vulnerable package.",
